    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NXxXwmWLKGiLpnX8uKS4HS)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent: based on `main`, no dependencies.\n- Touches only `sp-see-also` (doc, `.el`, test); builds on merged #366 and #440.\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks.\n- Branch name is not number-prefixed (cloud sessions cannot rename it); rename by hand if you want it.\n\n## What already existed\n\n- The backlink view is already `M-x sp-see-also-show` (PR #440), buffer `*see-also*`, part \"Referenced by\".\n- It already merges the kinds `footnote`, `section`, `link` (id links, also those Vulpea knows), `parent` and `cite` (`#+reference:` citekey), each entry marked `[cite]`, `[link]`, ... and the small print counting each kind.\n- `sp-relationship-annotator` has nothing of this (it is the graph view), so no new buffer or mode was built.\n\n## What was missing (this PR)\n\n- Only litnotes were read as sources: a `[cite:@key]` or id link in a concept note or writing project never showed.\n- `[cite/t:@key]` (any citation style) and `[[cite:&key]]` were not matched.\n- Changes, in `sp-see-also`:\n  - new `sp-see-also-cite-dirs` (default notes folder + `sp-writing-projects`): ripgrep finds every Org note citing the key or linking the `id:`; Vulpea backlinks are added.\n  - new `sp-see-also--cite-regexp`: all styles, multi-cite `@a;@b`, prefix/suffix, `key2` not matched.\n  - without ripgrep: old behaviour (litnotes only) plus Vulpea backlinks.\n- Docs: bullet lists in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-see-also.org`.\n- Tests (Emacs 29.3): 2 new, 49 of 49 pass. `tools/check-tangle.sh` shows only this doc; other drift (`sp-litnotes-meta`, `sp-batch-report-test`) is an Org-version artifact, not committed.\n- Not done: vulpea-ui sidebar widget for citations (the `concept-usage` widget exists); no new keys (`C-; n A` already opens the view). `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n- Not run: the GUI or the real vault.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] In a litnote with `#+reference:`, `M-x sp-see-also-show` (or `C-; n A`): \"Referenced by\" lists notes that are not litnotes too\n- [ ] A note with `[cite/t:@key; @other p. 4]` shows an entry marked `[cite]` with the line as context; RET jumps to it\n- [ ] A note linking `[[id:...]]` to the litnote shows `[link]` in the same group\n- [ ] A note citing `@key2` (a longer key) is not listed\n- [ ] Speed on the real vault is acceptable (ripgrep over the notes folder)\n- [ ] Regression: a concept without a citekey still shows its footnote references\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAogkKS5ZXm1xMTJvL)_",
